JACCARD_EXPLANATION = """Jaccard Similarity (0 to 1): Measures the overlap of unique words (lexical overlap) between texts.
Higher values indicate more shared vocabulary. Ignores semantics.
  - 0.5+: High Overlap (Many common words)
  - 0.2-0.5: Moderate Overlap (Some shared terms)
  - < 0.2: Low Overlap (Few common words)"""
COSINE_EXPLANATION = """Cosine Similarity (ST / OpenAI) (0 to 1): Measures the angular closeness of text embeddings (semantic meaning).
Higher values indicate greater semantic similarity based on the chosen embedding model.
  - Default ST: Sentence Transformer ('all-MiniLM-L6-v2') - Good general-purpose semantic capture.
  - Fine-Tuned ST (Optional): A Sentence Transformer model fine-tuned on SOP-specific data (if path provided). Expected to give better domain-specific similarity.
  - OpenAI: 'text-embedding-ada-002' - OpenAI's embedding model (results may differ from ST).
Interpretation Guide (General ST Scores):
  - 0.9+: Very High Similarity (Likely paraphrases or identical meaning)
  - 0.7-0.9: High Similarity (Similar topics and concepts)
  - 0.5-0.7: Moderate Similarity (Related topics, some overlap)
  - 0.3-0.5: Low Similarity (Different topics, weak relation)
  - < 0.3: Very Low Similarity (Largely unrelated)"""
